Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

ASU has joined with Starbucks to offer the Starbucks College Achievement Plan. This program is based on the belief that everyone should have the opportunity to pursue an education. The College Achievement Plan is available to all of Starbucks' full- and part-time partners of every brand who are employed within the United States.


Through a unique collaboration with ASU’s research-driven, top-ranked online degree programs, eligible partners will have the opportunity to finish their bachelor’s degree. Juniors and seniors will receive full tuition reimbursement, and freshmen and sophomores will be eligible for a partial tuition scholarship and need-based financial aid for two years of full-time study. Partners will have no commitment to remain at the company past graduation.


View all of ASU's online programs at http://asuonline.asu.edu/.


For more information about the Starbucks College Achievement Plan, please visit http://asuonline.asu.edu/starbucks-and-arizona-state-university.


Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

